[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I'm Morten. I have previously contributed to the PNT project, and now want to see if I can help in Mathlib. I've started with a very simple simplification of some existing theorems according to the contribution guides. PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37695\">here</a></p>",
        "id": 583805291,
        "sender_full_name": "Morten Ness",
        "timestamp": 1775483541
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is it worthwhile to send PRs for tiny improvements? e.g.:</p>\n<p>Existing proof:<br>\ntheorem mem_closure_singleton_self (x : G) : x ∈ Subgroup.closure ({x} : Set G) := by<br>\n  simpa [-Subgroup.subset_closure] using Subgroup.subset_closure (k := {x})</p>\n<p>To:<br>\ntheorem mem_closure_singleton_self (x : G) : x ∈ Subgroup.closure ({x} : Set G) := by<br>\n  exact Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)</p>",
        "id": 583813297,
        "sender_full_name": "Morten Ness",
        "timestamp": 1775486925
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You should delete <code>by exact</code> because they cancel out. Does it still work then? I would definitely not make ten such PRs! It's not really achieving anything I guess. But maybe one is ok.</p>",
        "id": 583813851,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775487115
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this seem to work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_closure_singleton_self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subset_closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So it's not really a worthwhile pursuit to do these tiny cleanups? Or gather a bunch together in one PR?</p>",
        "id": 583814439,
        "sender_full_name": "Morten Ness",
        "timestamp": 1775487344
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another tiny example:</p>\n<p>Original:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux_rec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">if_neg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Simplified:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux_rec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">xgcdAux</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">if_neg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583815067,
        "sender_full_name": "Morten Ness",
        "timestamp": 1775487601
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1016825\">Morten Ness</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/New.20user/near/583813297\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is it worthwhile to send PRs for tiny improvements? e.g.:</p>\n<p>Existing proof:<br>\ntheorem mem_closure_singleton_self (x : G) : x ∈ Subgroup.closure ({x} : Set G) := by<br>\n  simpa [-Subgroup.subset_closure] using Subgroup.subset_closure (k := {x})</p>\n<p>To:<br>\ntheorem mem_closure_singleton_self (x : G) : x ∈ Subgroup.closure ({x} : Set G) := by<br>\n  exact Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The discussion in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/distinguishing.20different.20types.20of.20.60exact.60/with/580867616\">this thread</a> suggests that such a move might not be welcomed because this doesn't work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Lattice</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_closure_singleton_self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible_and_instances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subset_closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583821952,
        "sender_full_name": "A.",
        "timestamp": 1775489662
    },
